**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** How a kit names what it holds, and the one hash of bytes (001 §E 'References inside a kit are relative paths (forward slashes) plus the SHA-256 recorded at attach time', 'Absolute paths are never stored'; 001 §A 'Kit extensions'; 001 §P: `KitProxy` covers 'kit, items, setups, experiments, studies and fit runs'; .spec-md §5). (1) In `Kit.fs`, after `KitAccess` (step 122), each doc one to three lines: (a) `KitRelativePath of string`, a path inside a kit, with forward slashes. `static member tryCreate (text : string) : Result<KitRelativePath, KitError>` replaces every `\` with `/` and then refuses, with `InvalidKitPathErr` naming the text: an empty or white-space text; a rooted path (a leading `/`); a path holding a `:` (a drive such as `C:/data` or `C:data`); and a path any of whose `/`-separated segments is empty, `.` or `..`. Otherwise it answers the forward-slashed text, so a path is never absolute and never escapes the kit. No other normalisation is added. (b) `KitFileKind` = `ItemKitFile` | `SetupKitFile` | `ExperimentKitFile` | `StudyKitFile` | `FitRunKitFile`: the kit files that exist many times, one per item, setup, experiment, study and fit run (001 §A; the `.kit-json` is not a kind, because it has its own verbs). `member this.extension : FileExtension` answers `.item-json`, `.setup-json`, `.experiment-json`, `.study-json` and `.fitrun-json`; `member this.fileNameOf (stem : FileStem) : FileName` is `stem.withExtension this.extension` (step 24); `static member all : KitFileKind list` lists the five in that order. The kinds are stored only as their extensions, so no int tag, `tryOfWire` or other member is added. The sections that bring each kind's format (S4.3 experiments and setups, S7.1 items, S11 studies and fit runs) add no case and no proxy verb. (c) `KitFileText of string`, the text of a file in a kit: a kit file the app owns, or a lab file it only reads (001 §E), UTF-8 without a byte-order mark. One type serves both, because two would need a conversion each way (ELEV006). (d) `KitDataFile = { path : KitRelativePath; text : KitFileText; contentHash : ContentHash }`: a lab file as read, with the SHA-256 of its bytes as stored (001 §E). (e) `KitError` gains `MissingKitFileErr of reason : string` (the kit holds no file at that name or path) and `InvalidKitPathErr of reason : string`, rendered `the kit holds no such file: <reason>` and `the path is not inside the kit: <reason>`. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs`: `ContentHash` (step 24) gains `static member ofBytes (bytes : byte[]) : ContentHash`, the lowercase hex (`Convert.ToHexStringLower`) SHA-256 (`SHA256.HashData`) of the bytes. Its doc says it is the one SHA-256 body of the app, used for an entry's canonical content and for a kit's files. `ContentHash`'s doc names both uses. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/CanonicalJson.fs`: `contentHashOf` (step 27) hashes the UTF-8 bytes of the compact canonical rendering through `ContentHash.ofBytes`, and its own `SHA256.HashData` / `Convert.ToHexStringLower` lines are deleted: a move, so every hash is unchanged and step 27's frozen hash literal (`CanonicalJsonTests`, `the canonical form of a fixed value is frozen`) still holds. Tests. `KitTests` (step 122): `a kit-relative path keeps forward slashes and refuses an absolute or escaping path`: `data\raw\run 1.csv` answers `data/raw/run 1.csv`, and `data/raw/run 1.csv` and `.kit-json` are kept as given; `""`, `"  "`, `/data/a.csv`, `C:/a.csv`, `C:a.csv`, `../a.csv`, `data/../../a.csv`, `data/./a.csv` and `data//a.csv` each answer `InvalidKitPathErr`. `every kit file kind renders its 001 extension and names its files`: the five extensions exactly as above, `all` in that order, and `ExperimentKitFile.fileNameOf (FileStem "CPL-(QZ#45-LR#45)-CPL")` is `FileName "CPL-(QZ#45-LR#45)-CPL.experiment-json"`. `every kit error renders its condition and its payload` (step 122) also covers the two new cases. `LibraryEntryFilesTests` (step 24) gains `the content hash of bytes is their lowercase SHA-256`: `ContentHash.ofBytes` of the UTF-8 bytes of `abc` is `ContentHash "ba7816bf8f01cfea414140de5dae2223b00361a396177a9cb410ff61f20015ad"`, and of no bytes `ContentHash "e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"`.

**Acceptance.** After the path, kind and hash types land, `KitRelativePath.tryCreate` MUST refuse every absolute or escaping path and `contentHashOf` MUST hash through `ContentHash.ofBytes` with every hash unchanged; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a kit-relative path keeps forward slashes and refuses an absolute or escaping path`, `every kit file kind renders its 001 extension and names its files`, `the content hash of bytes is their lowercase SHA-256` and the widened `every kit error renders its condition and its payload`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the eleven s15 invariants MUST pass.
